From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:03:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 119/119] Bluetooth: add an experimental MT6797 CONSYS HCI
 driver

Register one HCI device on the btmt6797 platform device that the CONSYS
owner creates. Open attaches to the persistent STP link and close
detaches. Send passes the H:4 packet, type byte first, to STP task 0,
waiting up to 1 s for queue room. Received task-0 payloads are copied in
hard IRQ context into a bounded 16-slot ring, refused when it is full so
the controller resends, and reassembled into events, ACL and SCO in a
work item, since H:4 packets need not align with STP frames.

A link failure or a malformed H:4 stream is reported to the core as a
hardware error. No vendor init script, sleep, radio setting or address
write is sent; there is no set_bdaddr hook.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
